## Pull request overview

This PR introduces a simplified alert creation wizard for Error Tracking, designed to improve user experience and increase conversion rates. The wizard provides a guided 3-step flow (Destination → Trigger → Configure) as an alternative to the existing template-based approach. Key improvements include proper OAuth redirect handling for Slack and GitHub integrations, smart destination sorting based on usage patterns, and comprehensive analytics tracking to measure the impact through A/B testing.

**Changes:**
- Added new AlertWizard component with 3-step guided flow for creating error tracking alerts
- Fixed GitHub OAuth redirects to properly preserve query parameters and navigation context
- Enhanced Slack redirect handling to maintain query parameters through OAuth flow
- Implemented smart destination sorting that prioritizes previously used integrations
- Added comprehensive analytics tracking for wizard usage and conversion measurement

### Reviewed changes

Copilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated no comments.

<details>
<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>

| File | Description |
| ---- | ----------- |
| ErrorTrackingAlerting.tsx | Main integration point that wraps wizard logic and switches between wizard/traditional views based on feature flag |
| alertWizardLogic.ts | Core wizard state management including step navigation, template loading, alert creation, and URL synchronization |
| AlertWizard.tsx | Main wizard component with stepper, step rendering, and navigation controls |
| TriggerStep.tsx | Step component for selecting alert trigger (issue created/reopened) |
| DestinationStep.tsx | Step component for selecting notification destination with smart sorting and loading states |
| ConfigureStep.tsx | Step component for configuring destination-specific inputs with test functionality |
| WizardCard.tsx | Reusable card component for selectable options in wizard steps |
| AlertWizardStepper.tsx | Progress indicator showing current step and allowing navigation to completed steps |
